Your project targets **.NET 10** and `ReportGenerator.cs` has the filesystem statics you mentioned (plus `DateTime.UtcNow`, `Environment.*`, and `Console.*`). Here's the recommended approach for the **filesystem** calls:

## Use `System.IO.Abstractions` (NuGet)

This is the battle-tested library for making `File.*` and `Directory.*` testable. Don't roll a custom wrapper.

### 1. Install the package

```
dotnet add package System.IO.Abstractions
```

### 2. Inject `IFileSystem` into your class

```csharp
using System.IO.Abstractions;

public class ReportGenerator(IFileSystem fileSystem)
{
    public string GenerateReport(string reportName)
    {
        var outputDir = "/tmp/reports";

        if (!fileSystem.Directory.Exists(outputDir))
            fileSystem.Directory.CreateDirectory(outputDir);

        var reportPath = fileSystem.Path.Combine(outputDir, $"{reportName}.txt");
        fileSystem.File.WriteAllText(reportPath, $"Report: {reportName}");

        return reportPath;
    }
}
```

### 3. Register in DI

```csharp
// In Program.cs:
builder.Services.AddSingleton<IFileSystem, FileSystem>();
```

### 4. Test with `MockFileSystem`

```
dotnet add <TestProject> package System.IO.Abstractions.TestingHelpers
```

```csharp
using System.IO.Abstractions.TestingHelpers;

[Test]
public void GenerateReport_CreatesFile()
{
    var mockFs = new MockFileSystem();
    mockFs.AddDirectory("/tmp/reports");
    var generator = new ReportGenerator(mockFs);

    var path = generator.GenerateReport("Sales");

    Assert.True(mockFs.File.Exists(path));
    Assert.Contains("Sales", mockFs.File.ReadAllText(path));
}
```

### Key points

- `IFileSystem` wraps `File.*`, `Directory.*`, and `Path.*` — covers all three of your statics in one abstraction
- `MockFileSystem` provides an in-memory filesystem for tests — no temp files, no cleanup
- Register as **singleton** (it's stateless)

> **Bonus:** Your `ReportGenerator` also has `DateTime.UtcNow`, `Environment.*`, and `Console.*`. On .NET 10, use the built-in **`TimeProvider`** for time, and consider lightweight custom wrappers for Environment/Console if you want those testable too. Want me to generate those as well?
